**Reused Evidence**
None. No previously indexed 7B evidence item was reusable without stretching beyond the 7B admissibility gate.

**New Evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-08-10","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00007.html","claim":"Kishida said he personally had no links to the former Unification Church to the best of his knowledge, told ministerial candidates to examine any connections, and said he appointed only those who agreed to review the ties.","locator":"lines 60-63","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO transcript with direct contemporaneous statements by the prime minister.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Direct Kishida public statement and cabinet-management instruction; the truth of the personal no-links claim remains unverified within this source.","contrary_evidence":["Later reporting showed some newly appointed ministers still had church links, which undercuts the claim that vetting was fully effective."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.5","7B.6","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"5 members of Kishida's new Cabinet had links with Unification Church","publisher":"Kyodo News","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://english.kyodonews.net/articles/-/35165","claim":"At least five members of Kishida's new Cabinet had relations with the Unification Church despite a reshuffle aimed at purging links, and Kishida said he had appointed only those who agreed to review their ties.","locator":"opening paragraphs 1-3","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous reporting with named cabinet admissions and a quoted Kishida statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"This reflects Kishida's cabinet-selection and vetting choices, but the article does not show personal financial benefit or direct self-dealing by Kishida.","contrary_evidence":["The article relies on self-disclosures by cabinet members and does not independently audit every relationship it reports."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan govt calls for officials to review ties with Unification Church","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/08/22/japan-politics-church","claim":"A government spokesperson said cabinet members need to check and review their ties with the Unification Church to alleviate public concerns.","locator":"lead paragraph and quoted Cabinet Secretary Matsuno line","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on an official government briefing, with a direct quotation from the cabinet spokesperson.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Government response under Kishida's administration after notice of the scandal; it shows an official review response rather than personal enrichment.","contrary_evidence":["This is a remedial response, not proof that earlier vetting or disclosure was adequate."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan ruling party says 179 of 379 lawmakers had interactions with Unification Church","publisher":"Reuters via Yahoo News","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/japan-ruling-party-says-179-083452862.html","claim":"A party investigation found that 179 of 379 LDP lawmakers had interactions with the Unification Church and 17 received election help.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on an LDP internal investigation, with specific numbers and election-help detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Party-level network evidence under Kishida's leadership; it does not by itself establish Kishida's personal profit or hidden assets.","contrary_evidence":["This is organizational and factional evidence, not direct proof of Kishida's own personal wrongdoing."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-08-31","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202208/_00031.html","claim":"Kishida apologized for the Unification Church links, ordered public disclosure of LDP member checks, directed all LDP Diet members to sever ties, and announced government victim-relief coordination.","locator":"lines 37-51","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO transcript with direct apology, corrective orders, and concrete remedial steps.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Direct Kishida response after the scandal became public; the apology and directives are his own public actions.","contrary_evidence":["The same statement acknowledges continuing public doubt and media criticism, so it is correction under pressure rather than clean exoneration."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan PM orders probe into Unification Church links to ruling party members","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/japan-pm-orders-probe-into-unification-church-links-to-ruling-party-members-2913437","claim":"Kishida ordered an investigation into the Unification Church under the Religious Corporations Act, apologized that many LDP members' ties undermined public trust, and said the government would clarify the situation and protect victims.","locator":"lead paragraphs and quoted Kishida remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with direct quotation and specific administrative action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Direct Kishida action after public notice of the scandal and its fallout.","contrary_evidence":["The report also shows the controversy remained broad and unresolved within the ruling party."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Japan PM defends decision on state funeral for Abe","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-09","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/09/japan-politics-unification-church-kishida","claim":"Kishida accepted criticism that his explanation for the state funeral was insufficient and said he would provide a thorough explanation, while public opposition was tied in part to church-link revelations.","locator":"lines 653-656","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report with Kishida's own admission that the explanation was insufficient.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"This is a direct public-correction episode by Kishida, but it concerns policy justification more than financial honesty or private gain.","contrary_evidence":["The issue is indirect to personal integrity and does not itself demonstrate self-dealing or deliberate lying."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida","publisher":"Prime Minister's Office of Japan","publication_date":"2022-12-10","url":"https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202212/_00004.html","claim":"Kishida said he met people harmed by the former Unification Church, instructed officials to create a new law with the greatest regulation possible under constitutional limits, and set up a government-wide team to help victims use the new system.","locator":"lines 37-41 and 51","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary PMO transcript with concrete remedial instructions and implementation planning.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Direct Kishida response after notice of harm, using executive and legislative authority to create remedy.","contrary_evidence":["This is reactive remediation, not proof that earlier party vetting or disclosure was adequate."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Cabinet approved the bill to prevent improper solicitation of donations by corporations and similar bodies","publisher":"Consumer Affairs Agency, Government of Japan","publication_date":"2022-12-01","url":"https://www.caa.go.jp/notice/entry/031340/","claim":"The page records the December 1, 2022 cabinet decision approving the bill to prevent improper solicitation of donations by corporations and similar bodies.","locator":"title and publication date at the top of the notice","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Japanese government notice of the cabinet decision; the claim is narrow and date-specific.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, contemporaneous","ruler_attribution":"Cabinet-level action under Kishida's administration; the page does not isolate Kishida's personal role beyond government direction.","contrary_evidence":["The notice is formal and thin on implementation details or measurable results."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Consumer policy white paper section on the former Unification Church donation-law response","publisher":"Consumer Affairs Agency, Government of Japan","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.caa.go.jp/policies/policy/consumer_research/white_paper/2023/white_paper_204.html","claim":"The white paper says that Kishida's August 2022 instruction triggered interagency coordination, a justice-minister-led liaison meeting, and a consumer-affairs expert process that analyzed complaint data and recommended stronger relief and reporting powers.","locator":"lines 163-164","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government retrospective summarizing the 2022 policy response and its administrative steps.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"retrospective summary of 2022 actions; published after the target year","ruler_attribution":"Government-wide implementation summary under Kishida's instruction; not a direct finding on personal honesty, but strong on response mechanics.","contrary_evidence":["It is retrospective and still does not quantify how fully victims were helped in 2022."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I reviewed roughly 25-40 documents across official PMO transcripts, Consumer Affairs Agency notices and white paper material, Reuters/Kyodo/AP coverage, and later retrospectives. I kept the most directly attributable 2022 items and rejected or de-emphasized:

- Duplicate Reuters syndications that repeated the same church-story facts without adding new attribution.
- Broad background explainers on the Unification Church that were useful context but not ruler-specific enough to carry weight by themselves.
- 2023 fundraising-scandal coverage, because it is out of period for the 2022 dossier even though it is relevant to Kishida's later integrity record.
- Country-level corruption and accountability indicators, because they are context only and do not prove personal honesty or self-dealing.
- State-funeral reporting beyond the single admission that the explanation was insufficient, because the rest of the coverage sits closer to 4B/3B than to personal integrity.
- Any items that repeated the same remedial action in slightly different language without adding a new claim or locator.

**Remaining Gaps**
- There is still no direct 2022 evidence of Kishida's own private financial self-enrichment, hidden assets, or personal campaign-finance abuse.
- The evidence is much stronger on party/network conduct and corrective response than on Kishida's personal benefit from office.
- More search would help on formal asset declarations, donations, private interests, and whether any 2022 appointments or decisions were tied to Kishida's own allies, donors, or family.
- I also do not have a strong independent audit of whether his church-related vetting and disclosure instructions were actually followed across the cabinet and ruling party by year-end 2022.

No score assigned.
